meta {
  name: Slack Notify
  type: http
  seq: 69
}

post {
  url: http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/v1/slack/notify
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "apikey": "",
    "message": "Test alert from OpenAlgo API",
    "wait_for_delivery": false
  }
}

docs {
  Post a message to the Slack channel whose incoming webhook is saved on the
  /slack page. Slack alerts must be switched on at /alerts.

    "message":            the text, at most 4000 characters
    "wait_for_delivery":  false (default) queues the message and returns at once;
                          true posts it first and reports whether Slack took it

  Slack's control characters & < > are escaped, so a message cannot mention a
  whole channel or hide a link behind other text. Bold with *single asterisks*
  still works.

  The webhook URL itself is never sent or returned by the API. Saving,
  replacing and removing it is done on the session-authenticated /slack page.
}
